      "text": "Let the cost of a X-pen and Y-pencil be represented by 100x + y. Since each pen has equal price and each pencil has equal price, we can write the following two equations from the given conditions:\n\n4(100x + y) = 2.24 * 100 or 400x + 4y = 224;     equation (i)\n2(100x + y) = (1.54) * 100 or 200x + 2y = 154;  equation (ii)\n\nMultiplying equation (ii) by 2 and equation (i) by 3, we get:\n\n200x + 4y = 308                      3(200x + 2y = 154); equation (iii)\n3(400x + 4y) = 3(224);                1200x+12y = 672;  equation (iv)\n\nSubtracting equation (iii) from equation (iv), we obtain:\n\n1200x + 12y - 3(200x + 2y) = 672  800x = 672;    x = 0.84\n           4y = 224 - 0.84*4         y = 0.76\n\nThus, the cost of a pen and a pencil is 84 cents and 76 cents respectively.",
