    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "Given the programmed solutions for four pens and three pencils cost $2.24, 2.24 is converted to cents and equals 224. Similarly, two pens plus five pencils costs 1.54, 1.54 is converted to cents and equals 154. Consequently, the price of a pencil is $C$ and the price of a pen is $P$. You have two equations: $4P + 3C = 224$ and $2P + 5C = 154$. To solve for $C$, perform the following operations:\n\n$$\\begin{array}{|rcll|}\n\\hline\n4P + 3C &=& 224 \\quad & [\\text{One equation}] \\\\\n2P + 5C &=& 154 \\quad & [\\text{Another equation}] \\\\\n\\hline\n2\\times & (2P + 5C) &=& 2\\times154\n\\\\ & (4P + 10C) &=& 2 \\times 154\n\\\\ & & \\quad 4P + 10C-4P &=& 308-4P\n\\\\ & & \\quad 3C &=& 308-4P\n\\\\ & & \\quad 152-4P &=& 3C\n\\\\ & & \\quad 4P &=& 152-3C\n\\\\ & & \\quad 4P &=& \\frac{152-C}{3}\n\\\\ & & \\quad 4P &=& 152 \\times\\frac{1}{3} - \\frac{C}{3}\n\\\\ & & \\quad 4P &=& \\frac{152}{3} - \\frac{C}{3}\n\\\\ & & \\quad \\mathbf{P &=& \\frac{152-3C}{12}} \\\\\n\\hline\n\\end{array}$$\n\nSubstitute: $4P+3C=224$ into $4P+3C=224$. The result of the substitution is:\n\n$$152 - C - 3C = 224$$\n$$152 - 4C = 224$$\n$$-4C = 224 - 152$$\n$$-4C = 72$$\n$$C = \\mathbf{18}$$\n\nConclusion: The cost of a pencil is $\\boxed{18}$ cents.",
